dragonfixes.research_page.witchwood_rod=Your studies into other schools of magic have led you to discover an unusual tree known as Witchwood. Unlike Silverwood, which has a natural affinity for Vis, Witchwood appears to be particularly receptive to mana. Feeling experimental, you attempted to infuse it with purified Vinteum dust.<BR><BR>Your first results were catastrophic, but after reinforcing the rod with some Ent twigs, you have managed to create a rod capable of converting mana into Vis.<BR><BR>And it paid off! The resulting wand can store %d vis of each primal aspect. On top of that, it gradually replenishes its reserves by drawing upon your mana! Unfortunately, it is not very efficient: it costs 140 mana per point of vis.<BR><BR>Further research may reveal ways to improve its efficiency...
dragonfixes.research_page.witchwood_staff=Witchwood reacts poorly to elemental crystals, making the creation of a staff difficult and reducing its capacity to %d vis of each primal aspect.<BR><BR>In return, the staff channels mana into vis more efficiently and recharges more than twice as quickly as the wand when carried in your hotbar.
dragonfixes.research_page.vinteum_cap=Vinteum is a more ordered form of Thaumium, allowing its magical potential to be used without infusion. While its vis discount is comparable to Thaumium, it also reduces the mana consumed by a Witchwood wand or staff during self-recharging.
